#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:1
msgid "Layouts, Tiling, and Partitions by Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:3
msgid ""
"cute-layout and cute-rs let you describe how logical coordinates map to "
"physical memory: whether that is a 1D vector split across threads, a row-"
"wise reduction across warps, or a 2D swizzled shared-memory tile shared by "
"host TMA encoding and device MMA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:7
msgid "1. Evaluating Layouts with cute-layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:9
msgid ""
"cute-layout is a `no_std` crate shared by both cute-rs and the compiler. A "
"`Layout` pairs a shape `IntTuple` with a stride `IntTuple` and maps logical "
"coordinates to linear offsets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:11
msgid ""
"use cute_layout::{IntTuple, Layout};\n"
"\n"
"// Shape (2, 3) with row-major stride (3, 1)\n"
"let layout: Layout = \"(2,3):(3,1)\".parse().unwrap();\n"
"assert_eq!(layout.checked_call(&IntTuple::Leaf(1)), Some(3));\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:19
msgid ""
"In kernel signatures, you write static layouts as Rust type markers (`C<N>`, "
"Rust tuples such as `(A, B)` for nested modes, `Layout<Shape, Stride>`, "
"`RowMajor<R, C>`, `ColMajor<R, C>`, `Swizzle<B, M, S>`, and "
"`ComposedLayout<Swizzle, Offset, Layout>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:23
msgid "2. 1D Tiling and Ragged Tails (zipped_divide and slice)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:25
msgid ""
"`zipped_divide::<TILE>()` restructures a flat 1D tensor into a 2D view "
"indexed by `(offset_inside_tile, tile_number)`. Calling `.slice(tid)` "
"selects the tile owned by thread `tid`. `local_tile::<TILE>(tile)` is the "
"one-call form, equal to `zipped_divide::<TILE>().slice(tile)`: CuTe's "
"`local_tile` for a one-dimensional tiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:31
msgid ""
"`zipped_divide::<4>()` and `.slice(tid)` partition a 1,003-element vector "
"across 251 threads: threads `0..249` take the vectorized `cute.copy` path, "
"while thread `250` runs a scalar loop over the 3-element tail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:34
msgid ""
"let tid = thread::index_1d().get();\n"
"let g_a = cute_rs::Tensor::from_slice(a).zipped_divide::<4>();\n"
"let g_b = cute_rs::Tensor::from_slice(b).zipped_divide::<4>();\n"
"let g_c = cute_rs::TensorMut::from_disjoint_slice(&mut c).zipped_divide::"
"<4>();\n"
"\n"
"let t_a = g_a.slice(tid);\n"
"let t_b = g_b.slice(tid);\n"
"let mut t_c = g_c.slice(tid);\n"
"\n"
"if t_a.is_full() {\n"
"    let sum = unsafe { t_a.load() } + unsafe { t_b.load() };\n"
"    unsafe { t_c.store(sum) };\n"
"} else {\n"
"    let mut k = t_a.base();\n"
"    while k < a.len() {\n"
"        unsafe { t_c.store_at(k, a[k] + b[k]) };\n"
"        k += 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:58
msgid "3. Shared Host/Device TMA Layout Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:60
msgid ""
"For 2D and 3D Tensor Memory Accelerator (TMA) transfers, you define the "
"swizzled shared-memory layout type **once** and use it on both the host and "
"the device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:66
msgid ""
"A single `ComposedLayout<Swizzle, Offset, Layout>` type alias binds host "
"`create_tensor_map_tiled` encoding to device `&TensorMap<T, Layout>` and "
"`Sm100SharedTile`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:69
msgid ""
"use cute_rs::copy::tma::{TmaEncodeOptions, "
"create_tensor_map_tiled_with_options};\n"
"use cute_rs::{ComposedLayout, RowMajor, Swizzle, TensorMap};\n"
"\n"
"// Shared layout type: 128x64 tile with a 128-byte swizzle\n"
"pub type ASmem = ComposedLayout<Swizzle<3, 3, 3>, 0, RowMajor<128, 64>>;\n"
"\n"
"// 1. Host: encode the 128-byte hardware CUtensorMap from `ASmem`\n"
"let a_desc: TensorMap<f16, ASmem> = create_tensor_map_tiled_with_options(\n"
"    a_dev.as_device_ptr(),\n"
"    m,\n"
"    k,\n"
"    k,\n"
"    TmaEncodeOptions::default(),\n"
")?;\n"
"\n"
"// 2. Device: receive the descriptor by value via #[grid_constant]\n"
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn gemm_kernel(#[grid_constant] a: &TensorMap<f16, ASmem>) {\n"
"    // `a` is guaranteed to carry the exact `ASmem` tile shape and swizzle\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/layouts-and-tiling.md:92
msgid ""
"If a kernel attempts to pass `&TensorMap<f16, ASmem>` into a copy or MMA "
"expecting a different layout or element type, rustc rejects the program at "
"compile time before device codegen even runs."
msgstr ""
